                          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure for Kan complexes
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %li
                %a{:href => "#coherent_vs_incoherent_idempotents"} Coherent vs incoherent idempotents
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+complete+category"} idempotent complete
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karoubi+envelope"} Karoubi complete
            or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+completion"} Cauchy complete
            , if every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent"} idempotent
            splits. Since the splitting of an idempotent is a limit
            %em or
            colimit of that idempotent, any category with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+complete+category"} all finite limits
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+cocomplete+category"} all finite colimits
            is idempotent complete.
          %p
            In an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            the idea is the same, except that the notion of
            %em idempotent
            is more complicated. Instead of just requiring that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi e
                    %mo =
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e\circ e = e
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi e
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e\circ e \simeq e
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi e
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi e
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e\circ e\circ e \simeq e
            are equivalent, and so on up. In particular,
            %em being idempotent
            is no longer a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff%2C+structure%2C+property"} property
            of a morphism, but
            %em structure
            on it.
          %p
            It is still true that a splitting of an idempotent in an
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Idem
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Idem^+
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/walking+structure"} free 1-category containing a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retraction"} retraction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e:X\to X
              the idempotent,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r:X\to Y
              the retraction, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i:Y\to X
              the section (and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo =
                    %mi i
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e = i r
              and
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r i = 1_Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Idem
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Idem
              be the similar nerve of the free 1-category containing an idempotent, which is the full sub-simplicial set of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Idem
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Idem^+
              spanned by the object
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ret
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ret
              be the image in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Idem
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Idem^+
              of the 2-simplex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Idem
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^2 \to Idem^+
              exhibiting the composite
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r i = 1_Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ret
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ret
              is also the quotient of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^2
              that collapses the 1-face to a point.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, 4.4.5.2 p.304
            )
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Let C be an
              = succeed "-category," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  An
                  %strong idempotent morphism
                  in C is a map of simplicial sets
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Idem
                          %mo →
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Idem \to C
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Fun
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Idem
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fun(Idem, C)
                  as the
                  %strong
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                    \-category of idempotents
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %li
                %p
                  A
                  %strong weak retraction diagram
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Ret
                          %mo →
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ret \to C
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Fun
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Ret
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fun(Ret, C)
                  as the
                  %strong
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                    \-category of weak retraction diagrams
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %li
                %p
                  A
                  %strong strong retraction diagram
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  is a map of simplicial sets
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Idem
                            %mo +
                          %mo →
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Idem^+ \to C
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Fun
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Idem
                        %mo +
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fun(Idem+, C)
                  as the
                  %strong
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                    \-category of strong retraction diagrams
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, 4.4.5.4 p.304
            )
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              An idempotent
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Idem
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon Idem \to C
              is
              %strong effective
              if it extends to a map
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Idem
                        %mo +
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Idem^+ \to C
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, above corollary 4.4.5.14
            )
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              An idempotent diagram
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Idem
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon Idem \to C
              is effective precisely if it admits an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limit"} (∞,1)-limit
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} (∞,1)-colimit
          %p
            By (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, lemma 4.3.2.13
            ).
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is called an
              %strong
                idempotent complete
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              if every idempotent is effective.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, above corollary 4.4.5.14
            )
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p The following properties generalize those of idempotent-complete 1-categories.
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} small (∞,1)-category
              is idempotent-complete if and only if it is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} accessible
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, 5.4.3.6
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} small (∞,1)-category
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Yoneda+embedding"} (∞,1)-Yoneda embedding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi Ind
                      %mi κ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to C' \hookrightarrow Ind_\kappa(C)
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'
              the full subcategory on
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} compact object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C'
              as the idempotent completion of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, lemma 5.4.2.4
          %h2#coherent_vs_incoherent_idempotents Coherent vs incoherent idempotents
          %p
            We may also ask how idempotent-completeness of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is related to that of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h C
            is an “incoherent idempotent” in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e:X\to X
            such that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ∼
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \sim e^2
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_3 Theorem
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Algebra"} HA
                Lemma 1.2.4.6)
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} stable
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is idempotent-complete (i.e. every coherent idempotent is effective) if and only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h C
              is (as a 1-category).
          %p
            However, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is not stable, this is false. The following counterexample in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGpd"} ∞Gpd
            is constructed in Warning 1.2.4.8 of
            = succeed "." do
